+# STO Linux Command 10.0.4
 
-A native Rust **AetherForge Dragon Glass launcher and compatibility manager for the official Arc client and Star Trek Online on Linux**. **10.0.3 synchronizes STO Linux Command with the AetherForge OS 10.0.3 release line** while carrying forward the complete v1.19.0 Arc Account Hybrid, first-class Arc install/run workflow, and direct STO launch path unchanged.
+A native Rust **AetherForge Dragon Glass launcher and compatibility manager for the official Arc client and Star Trek Online on Linux**. **10.0.4 continues from the AetherForge-synchronized 10.0.3 baseline** and adds contained STO gameplay plus an authoritative visual-stability pipeline while preserving Arc/account separation and direct UMU + GE-Proton play.
 
 The native launcher never asks for, stores, scrapes, or logs Arc passwords, cookies, account tokens, or private authentication payloads.
 
@@ -14,6 +14,18 @@
 
 
 
+
+## v10.0.4: Embedded STO + Visual Stability
+
+10.0.4 keeps Star Trek Online inside the STO Linux Command window instead of launching a normal detached desktop game window. PLAY remains Arc-independent: the launcher applies its selected visual profile, safely patches the verified STO display keys in `GamePrefs.Pref`, writes a launcher-owned DXVK configuration, starts nested Gamescope, and runs the canonical UMU + GE-Proton direct plan inside it.
+
+- **Embedded STO viewport:** nested Gamescope is forced onto X11/XWayland and reparented into the AetherForge launcher with xdotool. The child surface is moved/resized with the live egui viewport.
+- **No detached fallback:** if Gamescope, xdotool, or an X11/XWayland `DISPLAY` is unavailable, PLAY blocks with an actionable error instead of spawning STO outside the launcher. If reparenting times out, the launch process group is terminated.
+- **Visual Stability is authoritative:** the selected Visual Stability / Low Latency / Compatibility profile is reapplied before every PLAY. The launcher detects display geometry/refresh, writes `DXVK_CONFIG_FILE`, and never enables Gamescope `--immediate-flips`.
+- **Safe STO gamefile integration:** before modification, `Live/localdata/GamePrefs.Pref` is backed up. Only verified keys are managed: `GfxSettings.Fullscreen`, `GfxSettings.ScreenWidth`, and `GfxSettings.ScreenHeight`; unknown settings/comments are preserved. Settings includes **Restore Previous GamePrefs**.
+- **Local Arc installer import:** user-selected Windows Arc installers are MZ-validated, copied into launcher-managed cache, fingerprinted for installer-log evidence, and then run through the managed UMU + GE-Proton prefix. Proprietary Arc installer bytes are never included in STO Linux Command release artifacts.
+- **Direct PLAY remains frozen:** `build_direct_sto_launch_plan -> Gamescope -> UMU -> Star Trek Online.exe`, preserving `GAMEID=umu-default`, `STORE=none`, `PROTONPATH=GE-Proton`, and `PROTON_VERB=runinprefix`. Arc remains explicit install/account/patch/maintenance only.
+
 ## v10.0.3: AetherForge OS Synchronized Baseline
 
 10.0.3 establishes the canonical AetherForge-aligned release identity for STO Linux Command. The previous functional release **1.19.0 → 10.0.3** is an intentional release-line migration, not a downgrade or feature reset.
diff -ruN a/crates/sto-gui/src/embedded_game.rs b/crates/sto-gui/src/embedded_game.rs
--- a/crates/sto-gui/src/embedded_game.rs	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/crates/sto-gui/src/embedded_game.rs	2026-09-19 00:07:36.282687605 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,261 @@
+use std::{
+    env,
+    path::{Path, PathBuf},
+    process::Command,
+    time::{Duration, Instant},
+};
+
+const LAUNCHER_WINDOW_NAME: &str = "AetherForge STO Launcher";
+const ATTACH_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(15);
+
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct ViewportRect {
+    pub x: i32,
+    pub y: i32,
+    pub width: u32,
+    pub height: u32,
+}
+
+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
+pub struct EmbedPrerequisites {
+    pub gamescope: PathBuf,
+    pub xdotool: PathBuf,
+    pub display: String,
+}
+
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub enum EmbedEvent {
+    None,
+    Attached,
+    Exited,
+    Failed(String),
+}
+
+#[derive(Debug, Default)]
+pub struct EmbeddedGameController {
+    gamescope_pid: Option<u32>,
+    launcher_window: Option<String>,
+    child_window: Option<String>,
+    pending_since: Option<Instant>,
+    last_rect: Option<ViewportRect>,
+    full_view: bool,
+    error: Option<String>,
+}
+
+impl EmbeddedGameController {
+    pub fn begin_pending(&mut self, gamescope_pid: u32) {
+        self.gamescope_pid = Some(gamescope_pid);
+        self.launcher_window = None;
+        self.child_window = None;
+        self.pending_since = Some(Instant::now());
+        self.last_rect = None;
+        self.error = None;
+    }
+
+    pub fn is_running_or_pending(&self) -> bool {
+        self.gamescope_pid.is_some()
+    }
+
+    pub fn is_attached(&self) -> bool {
+        self.child_window.is_some()
+    }
+
+    pub fn gamescope_pid(&self) -> Option<u32> {
+        self.gamescope_pid
+    }
+
+    pub fn full_view(&self) -> bool {
+        self.full_view
+    }
+
+    pub fn toggle_full_view(&mut self) {
+        self.full_view = !self.full_view;
+        self.last_rect = None;
+    }
+
+    pub fn error(&self) -> Option<&str> {
+        self.error.as_deref()
+    }
+
+    pub fn poll(&mut self, xdotool: &Path) -> EmbedEvent {
+        let Some(pid) = self.gamescope_pid else {
+            return EmbedEvent::None;
+        };
+        if !process_exists(pid) {
+            self.reset();
+            return EmbedEvent::Exited;
+        }
+        if self.child_window.is_some() {
+            return EmbedEvent::None;
+        }
+
+        match self.try_attach(xdotool, pid) {
+            Ok(true) => EmbedEvent::Attached,
+            Ok(false) => {
+                if self.pending_since.is_some_and(|started| started.elapsed() >= ATTACH_TIMEOUT) {
+                    let message = "Gamescope started, but its X11/XWayland window could not be attached inside STO Linux Command. The detached host was terminated to preserve containment.".to_string();
+                    self.terminate();
+                    self.error = Some(message.clone());
+                    EmbedEvent::Failed(message)
+                } else {
+                    EmbedEvent::None
+                }
+            }
+            Err(error) => {
+                if self.pending_since.is_some_and(|started| started.elapsed() >= ATTACH_TIMEOUT) {
+                    let message = format!("Embedded STO attach failed: {error}");
+                    self.terminate();
+                    self.error = Some(message.clone());
+                    EmbedEvent::Failed(message)
+                } else {
+                    EmbedEvent::None
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    pub fn sync_rect(&mut self, xdotool: &Path, rect: ViewportRect) -> Result<(), String> {
+        let Some(child) = self.child_window.as_deref() else {
+            return Ok(());
+        };
+        if self.last_rect == Some(rect) {
+            return Ok(());
+        }
+        run_xdotool(
+            xdotool,
+            &["windowmove", "--sync", child, &rect.x.to_string(), &rect.y.to_string()],
+        )?;
+        run_xdotool(
+            xdotool,
+            &["windowsize", "--sync", child, &rect.width.to_string(), &rect.height.to_string()],
+        )?;
+        self.last_rect = Some(rect);
+        Ok(())
+    }
+
+    pub fn focus_game(&self, xdotool: &Path) -> Result<(), String> {
+        let child = self.child_window.as_deref().ok_or_else(|| "STO viewport is not attached yet".to_string())?;
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowfocus", "--sync", child])?;
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowraise", child])
+    }
+
+    pub fn release_mouse(&self, xdotool: &Path) -> Result<(), String> {
+        let launcher = self.launcher_window.as_deref().ok_or_else(|| "launcher X window is not known yet".to_string())?;
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowfocus", "--sync", launcher])
+    }
+
+    pub fn terminate(&mut self) {
+        if let Some(child) = self.child_window.as_deref() {
+            if let Some(xdotool) = find_program("xdotool") {
+                let _ = run_xdotool(&xdotool, &["windowclose", child]);
+            }
+        }
+        if let Some(pid) = self.gamescope_pid {
+            let process_group = format!("-{pid}");
+            let _ = Command::new("kill").args(["-TERM", "--", &process_group]).status();
+        }
+        self.gamescope_pid = None;
+        self.child_window = None;
+        self.launcher_window = None;
+        self.pending_since = None;
+        self.last_rect = None;
+    }
+
+    fn try_attach(&mut self, xdotool: &Path, gamescope_pid: u32) -> Result<bool, String> {
+        let launcher = match self.launcher_window.clone() {
+            Some(window) => window,
+            None => {
+                let window = find_window(
+                    xdotool,
+                    &["search", "--all", "--pid", &std::process::id().to_string(), "--name", "--limit", "1", LAUNCHER_WINDOW_NAME],
+                )?;
+                let Some(window) = window else { return Ok(false); };
+                self.launcher_window = Some(window.clone());
+                window
+            }
+        };
+
+        let child = find_window(
+            xdotool,
+            &["search", "--pid", &gamescope_pid.to_string(), "--onlyvisible", "--limit", "1", ".*"],
+        )?;
+        let Some(child) = child else { return Ok(false); };
+
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowreparent", &child, &launcher])?;
+        run_xdotool(xdotool, &["windowraise", &child])?;
+        self.child_window = Some(child);
+        self.last_rect = None;
+        Ok(true)
+    }
+
+    fn reset(&mut self) {
+        self.gamescope_pid = None;
+        self.launcher_window = None;
+        self.child_window = None;
+        self.pending_since = None;
+        self.last_rect = None;
+        self.full_view = false;
+    }
+}
+
+pub fn detect_prerequisites() -> Result<EmbedPrerequisites, String> {
+    let display = env::var("DISPLAY").map_err(|_| {
+        "Embedded STO requires an X11/XWayland DISPLAY. On Wayland, ensure XWayland is installed and enabled; detached fallback is intentionally disabled.".to_string()
+    })?;
+    if display.trim().is_empty() {
+        return Err("Embedded STO requires a non-empty X11/XWayland DISPLAY".into());
+    }
+    let gamescope = find_program("gamescope").ok_or_else(|| {
+        "Gamescope is required for embedded STO. On Arch: sudo pacman -S --needed gamescope".to_string()
+    })?;
+    let xdotool = find_program("xdotool").ok_or_else(|| {
+        "xdotool is required to reparent Gamescope into STO Linux Command. On Arch: sudo pacman -S --needed xdotool".to_string()
+    })?;
+    Ok(EmbedPrerequisites { gamescope, xdotool, display })
+}
+
+fn process_exists(pid: u32) -> bool {
+    Path::new("/proc").join(pid.to_string()).exists()
+}
+
+fn find_program(name: &str) -> Option<PathBuf> {
+    if name.contains('/') {
+        let path = PathBuf::from(name);
+        return path.is_file().then_some(path);
+    }
+    let path = env::var_os("PATH")?;
+    env::split_paths(&path)
+        .map(|dir| dir.join(name))
+        .find(|candidate| candidate.is_file())
+}
+
+fn find_window(xdotool: &Path, args: &[&str]) -> Result<Option<String>, String> {
+    let output = Command::new(xdotool)
+        .args(args)
+        .output()
+        .map_err(|error| format!("failed to run {}: {error}", xdotool.display()))?;
+    if !output.status.success() {
+        return Ok(None);
+    }
+    Ok(String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout)
+        .lines()
+        .map(str::trim)
+        .find(|line| !line.is_empty())
+        .map(str::to_string))
+}
+
+fn run_xdotool(xdotool: &Path, args: &[&str]) -> Result<(), String> {
+    let output = Command::new(xdotool)
+        .args(args)
+        .output()
+        .map_err(|error| format!("failed to run {}: {error}", xdotool.display()))?;
+    if output.status.success() {
+        return Ok(());
+    }
+    Err(format!(
+        "{} {} failed: {}",
+        xdotool.display(),
+        args.join(" "),
+        String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stderr).trim()
+    ))
+}
