+# STO Linux Command 10.0.4 Embedded STO + Visual Stability Design
+
+## Goal
+Keep Star Trek Online visually and interactively contained inside the STO Linux Command window while applying an authoritative visual-stability profile before every direct launch.
+
+## Frozen invariants
+- PLAY STO never opens Arc.
+- Direct STO remains UMU + GE-Proton with GAMEID=umu-default, STORE=none, PROTONPATH=GE-Proton, PROTON_VERB=runinprefix.
+- Arc remains a separate first-class maintenance/authentication surface.
+- STO Linux Command never stores Arc credentials or copies Arc session tokens.
+- The user-provided Arc installer is imported as a local executable; it is not redistributed in the launcher release.
+
+## Containment architecture
+On X11/XWayland, STO launches inside nested Gamescope. The Gamescope window is then reparented under the AetherForge STO Launcher top-level X window using xdotool. The launcher reserves a live viewport rectangle and continually keeps the reparented child positioned and sized to that rectangle. Keyboard/mouse focus moves into the child when the user focuses the viewport. Release Mouse returns focus to the launcher.
+
+Wayland does not expose general arbitrary foreign-surface embedding. On Wayland desktops the launcher therefore requires XWayland for containment. If the X11/XWayland containment prerequisites are missing, PLAY fails closed with an actionable message rather than spawning a separate STO desktop window.
+
+## Visual stability architecture
+A launcher-owned visual profile is persisted in ui.toml. The default is Visual Stability. Before each launch the launcher:
+1. Detects a usable display width, height, and refresh rate from kscreen-doctor, wlr-randr, or xrandr with safe fallback.
+2. Resolves a target frame rate from the selected profile.
+3. Writes a launcher-owned dxvk.conf and exports DXVK_CONFIG_FILE.
+4. Finds `Live/localdata/GamePrefs.Pref` relative to `Star Trek Online.exe`.
+5. Creates a timestamped backup before editing an existing GamePrefs file.
+6. Changes only verified STO preference keys: GfxSettings.Fullscreen, GfxSettings.ScreenWidth, GfxSettings.ScreenHeight. Unknown keys and comments are preserved byte-for-byte apart from line-ending normalization on edited lines.
+7. Launches nested Gamescope at the viewport resolution and target refresh, then launches the unchanged UMU direct-STO plan as Gamescope's child command.
+
+## Profiles
+- Visual Stability: DXVK tear-free enabled, sync interval controlled for stable presentation, max frame latency 1, nested refresh target three Hz below detected refresh when refresh is above 60 Hz, otherwise detected refresh.
+- Low Latency: no forced VSync, max frame latency 1, near-refresh target.
+- Compatibility: fixed synchronized presentation at detected refresh with no adaptive-sync request.
+
+The launcher never passes Gamescope `--immediate-flips`.
+
+## Game viewport UX
+While embedded STO is pending or active, the center content switches to a viewport page with a compact toolbar: state, target FPS, profile, Focus Game, Release Mouse, Full View, Exit Game. Full View expands the viewport within the same launcher window; it does not detach STO.
+
+When STO/Gamescope exits, the embedded child is detached/forgotten and the normal STO page returns.
+
+## Arc installer integration
+The existing local Arc installer path is promoted to an explicit Import Arc Installer flow. Local installers must exist and carry an MZ executable signature. The supplied installer fingerprint is recorded as known-good evidence for this build but is not required for future Arc installer updates. The installer runs through the same managed UMU + GE-Proton prefix.
+
+## Failure behavior
+- Missing Gamescope: block embedded PLAY and show the Arch install requirement.
+- Missing xdotool or DISPLAY/XWayland: block embedded PLAY; never fall back to a detached game window.
+- GamePrefs unavailable: continue with Gamescope/DXVK while reporting that the gamefile layer could not be applied.
+- Failed GamePrefs write: preserve original via backup and block only the gamefile mutation, not the backup.
+- Reparent timeout: terminate/close the Gamescope host instead of leaving a stray detached game window.
+
+## Verification
+Static Python regressions enforce source contracts in this sandbox. The host installer remains authoritative for cargo fmt, strict Clippy (`-D warnings`), cargo test, and release build because the sandbox has no Rust toolchain.
